From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:26:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: default the HEVC encoder maximum QP to 51
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_MAX_QP defaults to 0, and
s5p_mfc_set_enc_params_hevc() writes the minimum and maximum QP as the
QP bound. With the defaults every HEVC frame is coded at QP 0, whatever
bitrate the client asks for, and the frame QP controls are clamped to
[0, 0] until the client raises the maximum.

Default it to 51, the top of the range, as the H.264 maximum QP.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
index 3f8701e56..a82d22954 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
@@ -747,7 +747,7 @@ static struct mfc_control controls[] = {
 		.minimum = 0,
 		.maximum = 51,
 		.step = 1,
-		.default_value = 0,
+		.default_value = 51,
 	},
 	{
 		.id = V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_PROFILE,
